💡 Key Insights
A right-skewed, high-variance market: the price of houses is skewed (4.27) with a long tail stretching towards the higher values. The mean (538,932) is significantly higher than the median (450,000), suggesting the presence of luxury real estate affecting the average price.
3-4 bedroom homes dominate the market, comprising over 77% of all houses.
Presence of a waterfront increases the price of a house by an average of 3x (~1,641,902 vs ≈530,417 for houses without a waterfront), and this premium is consistent across all number of floors.
Living area has only a moderate correlation (0,62) with the price; 139 houses have a small area (in terms of the first quartile) but are in the top 25% by price, suggesting the importance of grade, waterfront, and location.
The price range spans 99.5x (78,000 to 7,700,000), indicating that the dataset encompasses both affordable homes and ultra-luxury estates, suitable for diverse budgets.
The location has a significant impact on the price, with the top postal code (122071) having an average house price of more than 4x higher than the average price of all houses in the dataset.
